// A recursive function whose signature is not fully inferred cannot be
// specialised (the self-call would name a definition that is never emitted),
// so codegen fails closed and asks for annotations. `walk` stays generic in its
// element type because nothing in the body inspects an element, and the two
// call sites instantiate it at two different ones.
fn walk(xs, n) = match n {
    0 => xs
    _ => walk(listReverse(xs), (n - 1) ?: 0)
}

fn main() = print("${listLength(walk([5, 6, 7], 2))} ${listLength(walk(["a", "b"], 1))}")
